description:
Letters from the clock: a fixed text sent to a mailbox. Leave out box to send to your own queue: the text then wakes you up as a user message. op is add, rm or ls. add takes exactly one of: every (every N cycles, stays), after (once, N cycles from now, then the entry removes itself), at (once at a wall-clock time, local time of the machine: "21:30", "2026-11-14 09:00" or "+10m" / "+2h"; then removes itself), cron (wall-clock times by a 5-field cron expression, local time: "0 9 * * 1" = Mondays 09:00; stays). Wall-clock entries are checked when the clock moves (at most one cycle late); missed while the tree slept = sent once on waking, and the letter says how late. Examples:
- wake me every 10 cycles: {"op": "add", "name": "check-inbox", "every": 10, "text": "Check data/ for new files."}
- wake me once at 21:30: {"op": "add", "name": "call", "at": "21:30", "text": "Send the report to ann."}
- every Monday 09:00: {"op": "add", "name": "monday", "cron": "0 9 * * 1", "text": "Weekly review is due."}
- remove one: {"op": "rm", "name": "check-inbox"}
- list all entries: {"op": "ls"}
Errors: ArgumentsBad, OpUnknown, EntryExists, EntryMissing, ClockMissing, ClockBad, RegisterBad, WriteFailed.
